==============================================================
Release Date:   18-MAR-2019
Release Type:   BUG
==============================================================

OVERVIEW:-
   - Fix release of GEM_GXL Release 1p12

CHANGES:-
   - DOCS      = NO
   - RTL       = YES
   - TB        = NO
   - TESTS     = YES
   - MODELS    = N/A
   - SCRIPTS   = YES
   - SW        = NO
   - FW        = NO

DOCUMENT:-
   - No change

ENHANCEMENT:-
   - Allowed 802.1Qav CBS to work concurrently with 802.3br pre-emption - gem_tx.v (ETH-1330)
   - Enabled dropping of 802.3br pre-empted frame if LPI is asserted between 802.3br frame fragments - gem_mmsl_rx_proc.v, gem_mmsl_rx_output_driver.v (ETH-1398)
   - Made it so a corrupted SMD-C will cause an 802.3br fragment to be dropped in the MMSL module rather than the receive MAC - gem_mmsl_rx_smd_decode.v (ETH-1411)
   - Removed the dependency wvalid has on awready in the AXI arbiter. The AXI arbiter is only present when 802.3br operation is configured - edma_axi_arbiter.v (ETH-1440)

BUG:-
   - Fixed bug in the AXI arbiter resulting in RREADY from the eMAC and pMAC clashing. The AXI arbiter is only present when 802.3br operation is configured - edma_axi_arbiter.v (ETH-1370)
   - Fixed bug where the last 802.3br frame fragment can be recognized as an intermediate frame fragment, resulting in the whole frame being dropped. This only occurs when the last two bytes of the frame CRC are "FFFF" which causes the CRC to be thought of as an mCRC - gem_mmsl_rx_proc.v (ETH-1331)
   - Fixed bug where 802.3br verify and respond packets do not obey the minimum IPG rules when data is being transmitted. If verify and respond packets were interspersed with transmitted frames then the IPG could have varied between one and twelve bytes - gem_mmsl_tx_proc.v (ETH-1158)
   - Fixed bug where perr was asserted for reads and writes to the 802.3br mmsl_int_enable (0x0F1C) and mmsl_int_disable (0x0F20) registers - gem_mmsl_reg.v (ETH-1166)
   - Fixed bug where when 802.3br pre-emption is disabled the IP core still responds to a verify packet - gem_mmsl_ver.v (ETH-1159)
   - Added missing synchronizer on the mdio_in signal going to the network status register at 0x0008 - gem_pclk_syncs.v, gem_reg_top.v (ETH-1455)

KNOWN LIMITATIONS:-
   - None

TOOL DEPENDENCY:-
   - None




