Name:           GEM_GXL
Part Number:    IP701X
Version Number: Release 1p11
==============================================================
Release Date:   23-JUN-2017
Release Type:   PLANNED
==============================================================

OVERVIEW:-
   - Q2 2017 release of GEM_GXL

CHANGES:-
   - DOCS      = YES
   - RTL       = YES
   - TB        = YES
   - TESTS     = YES
   - MODELS    = N/A
   - SCRIPTS   = YES
   - SW        = YES
   - FW        = YES

DOCUMENT:-
   - Updated user guide to revision 18
   - Included quick start guide
   - For IP7014A updated safety manual

ENHANCEMENT:-
   - Added ARQOS and AWQOS outputs for AXI QOS
   - Added 802.3br frame pre-emption capability for the FIFO interface
   - Added functionality to allow a user to drop frames on a queue if they exceed a certain frame length or to drop all frames matched by a particular type 2 screener if a programmed data-rate is exceeded. This is relevant to the 802.3Qci TSN standard.
   - Added ability to moderate interrupts so that the interrupt pin is only asserted after a programmable number of events have occured
   - Added ability to send PAUSE frames based on a configurable receive packet fill level
   - Added mechanism for flushing the receive FIFO on a per-queue basis
   - Added ability to specify time when a frame can be scheduled for transmission. This can be done on a per-frame basis as part of the transmit buffer descriptor.
   - Added new register to indicate PFC status
   - Added new status bit to the network status indicate AXI transactions are incomplete
   - Removed unnecessary interrupt classification output pins enet_int_fatal and enet_int_non_fatal
   - Added new output pins asf_int_fatal and asf_int_nonfatal
   - For IP7014A added new Automotive Safety Features (ASF) features:
       - Protection of configuration, control and status registers
       - Internal data and address path parity protection
       - Optional SECDED ECC for SRAM
       - Key logic duplication

BUG:-
   - Fixed MMSL interrupt not being connected at the top-level (ETH-793)
   - Fixed Error conditions not being latched in the mmsl status register (ETH-827)
   - 802.3br frame pre-emption - fixed mPacket mCRC not being correctly generated and checked (ETH-904)

KNOWN LIMITATIONS:-
   - Supports P802.1CB draft 2.4 frame elimination. The redundancy tag defined in later versions of the standard is not supported

TOOL DEPENDENCY:-
   - None


